{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:98bcb386dd9e3201","name":"The SoroSuub Corporation","source":{"id":"source:reference-98bcb386dd9e3201","title":"The SoroSuub Corporation","revision":26308,"timestamp":"2025-03-17T01:19:09Z","sha256":"c12cd0ad25f7bddbda6bcdcb55c4956306a803f1d699774140d32c509e3a3cbe","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26308","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20SoroSuub%20Corporation&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-98bcb386dd9e3201","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Because of SoroSuub's membership in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Commerce Guild"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Commerce_Guild","referenceId":"reference:9d27b12029ae3f0d"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sullust"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sullust","referenceId":"reference:0acf0480bb01d4e6"}," secedes from ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"}," at the beginning of the conflict and joins forces with ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"},". Given that nearly half of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sullustan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sullustan","referenceId":"reference:ad2946f5a1cb9e4b"}," population is employed by SoroSuub, there is practically no public outcry at this development. From this point onward, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sullust"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sullust","referenceId":"reference:0acf0480bb01d4e6"}," remains a strong supporter of the Confederacy. The planet itself is an important Confederacy fortress world, acting as a staging point for many invasions into the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Worlds"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Worlds?action=edit&redlink=1"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The end of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," and the emergence of the Empire brings about a subtle change on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sullust"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sullust","referenceId":"reference:0acf0480bb01d4e6"},". Although The SoroSuub Corporation maintained a great degree of control over the planet and the everyday lives of its citizens, it now governs the entire system and throws its industrial weight behind the Imperial war machine. Corporate Proclamation 137d dissolved the political Sullustan Council in favor of complete company rule allied with its principal client, the Empire.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
